# mm.camera.preview

Portable processing and button debounce for the PICO-Cam-A preview. The fixed
324x324 grayscale input maps to a 240x135 image using the reference's unscaled
crop (x=0..239, y=134..0), nearest sampling, fractional area averaging, or
area averaging with temporal history. Resizing modes reverse output rows
consistently with the crop. encode produces a complete big-endian RGB565 image
for a single LCD transfer. Button state accepts one falling edge or low level
after 30 ms of observed release, including taps latched while capture blocks
and unsigned timer wraparound.

The caller owns frame, image and button state. It resets temporal history on
restart or a mode change. The module does not access hardware or configure
sensor exposure. Output coordinates passed to sample must be in range.

Processing, encoding and debounce are project implementations. The default
crop coordinates and orientation follow Waveshare PICO-Cam-A/C/main.c. Host
regression coverage lives in tests/mm/camera/preview/ and uses the normal
mm.test runner:

```sh
sh test.sh --host tests/mm/camera/preview/
```
